        },
        "assignee": { "name": "Sophos MDR Team" },
        "overview": "INCIDENT SUMMARY\n\nAt 01:42 AM, a spearphishing email delivered a malicious Excel macro to sarah.chen (Finance). The macro downloaded a Cobalt Strike beacon establishing C2 with 185.220.101.47. At 02:31 AM, the attacker attempted lateral movement to SRV-FS01 (file server) using stolen svc-backup credentials. At 02:39 AM, ransomware deployment began — CryptoGuard blocked encryption.\n\nMDR RESPONSE\n• 02:39 AM — Alert triggered, MDR analyst assigned\n• 02:44 AM — Lateral movement blocked, SRV-FS01 protected\n• 02:47 AM — DESKTOP-FIN042 isolated from network\n• 03:15 AM — C2 IP blocked at firewall (185.220.101.47)\n• 03:30 AM — Compromised credentials (svc-backup) flagged for reset\n• 04:45 AM — Full remediation complete: malware removed, persistence cleared\n• 06:00 AM — Incident report delivered to customer\n\nIMPACT: 1 endpoint compromised (DESKTOP-FIN042). Lateral movement blocked before file server was reached. Zero data loss. Zero files encrypted (CryptoGuard). Estimated attacker dwell time: 57 minutes before containment.\n\nSTATUS: Contained. Awaiting customer approval to bring DESKTOP-FIN042 back online.",
        "detectionCount": 18,
        "escalated": true
      }
    ]
  },
